  "notes": "Covered timber toll bridge, 26 m long with 4.5 m between maple-plank walls, on river-cobble abutments, with a band of small windows, a shingle gable roof, a gabled portal at each end and a 2.5 m by 2.5 m toll booth beside the -Z portal. Long axis along local Z; base rim with the anchor on the deck row at mid-span, carves nothing.",
